<title>UK: HSBC leads $300 mln Hong Kong mortgage-backed bond.</title>
<headline>HSBC leads $300 mln Hong Kong mortgage-backed bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Markets said on Monday it was lead manager of a $300 million mortgage-backed FRN launched in the name of Hong Kong Sar Residential Mortgages Ltd.  </p>
<p>The originator of the receivables is Dah Sing Bank.</p>
<p>The notes are guaranteed by CAPMAC.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $300 MLN  BASE	 1M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *15.JUN.22</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **+20 BP    PAY DATE    26.JUN.97</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   0.35</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   REOFFER    PAR	 GOV LAW     HONG KONG</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 1    SALE LIMITS US/GB/HK/CI/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  0.125     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *EXPECTED MATURITY IS 15.MAR.04.</p>
<p>		EXPECTED AVERAGE LIFE IS 2.67 YEARS.</p>
<p>	    **CALL AT PAR ON 15.JUN.04 AFTER WHICH MARGIN OVER</p>
<p>		LIBOR RISES TO 45 B.P.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
